# {{FACTORY_NAME}}

A [jigs](https://salimhamed.github.io/jigs/) factory: workflows and the service that runs them.

## Start

```sh
cp .env.example .env
pnpm install
pnpm exec jigs up
pnpm exec jigs run hello --input message=hello
```

`jigs up` starts the service and ends by running `jigs doctor`, which checks
only what this factory's workflows use. `hello` needs no repository, ticket
source, credentials or agent. Rerun `jigs doctor` any time the service is up.
See [getting started](https://salimhamed.github.io/jigs/guide/getting-started).

Every `jigs` below means `pnpm exec jigs`. The service listens on
`:{{SERVICE_PORT}}`, its dashboard on `:{{DASHBOARD_PORT}}`, and Postgres on
`:{{POSTGRES_PORT}}`. `jigs status` lists runs; `jigs status <run-id>` shows one,
with the resources it recorded. All commands are in the
[CLI reference](https://salimhamed.github.io/jigs/guide/cli).

## Layout

- `jigs.config.ts` registers workflows, service settings, bindings, schedules
  and identities. Secrets live in `.env`.
- `jigs.ts` is generated step wrappers and bound blocks. Commit it, refresh it
  with `jigs generate`, and keep custom code elsewhere.
- `workflows/hello.ts` is the starter workflow. A workflow file has a
  `"use workflow"` function and a default export `{ workflow, inputs }`, plus
  `requires` when it needs integrations or agents.
- Add `blocks/` for reusable workflow-side code, and `steps/` for your own
  `"use step"` functions that do outside work.
- `jigs.config.test.ts` checks the registered workflows and compiled durable IDs.

Import with `#jigs`, `#blocks/<path>` and `#steps/<path>` from the `imports`
map in `package.json`; the workflow loaders in `jigs.config.ts` stay relative.
The API reference is also installed at `node_modules/@jigs-ai/jigs/docs/api/`,
one Markdown page per import path.

## Recipes

```sh
jigs recipe list
jigs recipe add ship
```

`recipe add` copies a recipe's workflow, tests and blocks into this factory and
keeps any file that already exists. Add the line it prints under `workflows` in
`jigs.config.ts`. The copied code is yours; upgrades never overwrite it. After
adding ship, read `blocks/delivery/README.md`. See
[recipes](https://salimhamed.github.io/jigs/guide/recipes).

## Verify and upgrade

```sh
pnpm typecheck
jigs build
pnpm test
```

Tests read the last build, so build first. `jigs up` applies changes to a
running service. `jigs upgrade` installs the latest release, refreshes
`jigs.ts`, runs `jigs up` and typechecks. Review and commit what it changes.

A workflow or step's file path and function name are its durable ID. Finish or
cancel active runs before renaming or moving either.
